    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. There's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`; the other two files are a base class and a helper), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Telephones.java`** \u2014 Added a `toDisplay(String e164)` helper (and a small `groupInThrees` helper). It splits the recognised country code off the front, then renders `\"+\" + code + \" \" + national-digits-grouped-in-threes`, e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. This lives in `Telephones` alongside the existing E.164 rules and country-code table it reuses.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Transient getTelephoneDisplay()` derived getter that delegates to `Telephones.toDisplay(this.telephone)`, matching the existing pattern for other derived owner fields.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `telephoneDisplay` read-only property to the `Owner` schema, so the openapi-generator produces the DTO field and MapStruct maps it automatically by name.\n\nThe acceptance test (`telephone` = `\"0412 345 678\"` \u2192 `telephone` `\"+61412345678\"`, `telephoneDisplay` `\"+61 412 345 678\"`) passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
